{
  "schema_version": "1.0.0",
  "edition_id": "WEBSTER1833",
  "book_code": "ECC",
  "chapter": 3,
  "verses": [
    {
      "id": "ECC.3.1",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ECC.3.1",
      "verse": 1,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "To every ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "thing there is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " a season, and a time to every purpose under the heaven:",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "ECC.3.2",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ECC.3.2",
      "verse": 2,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "A time to be born, and a time to die; a time to plant, and a time to pluck up ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "that which is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " planted;",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ECC.3.3",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ECC.3.3",
      "verse": 3,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "A time to kill, and a time to heal; a time to break down, and a time to build up;",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ECC.3.4",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ECC.3.4",
      "verse": 4,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "A time to weep, and a time to laugh; a time to mourn, and a time to dance;",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ECC.3.5",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ECC.3.5",
      "verse": 5,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "A time to cast away stones, and a time to gather stones; a time to embrace, and a time to refrain from embracing;",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ECC.3.6",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ECC.3.6",
      "verse": 6,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "A time to get, and a time to lose; a time to keep, and a time to cast away;",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ECC.3.7",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ECC.3.7",
      "verse": 7,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "A time to rend, and a time to sew; a time to keep silence, and a time to speak;",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ECC.3.8",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ECC.3.8",
      "verse": 8,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "A time to love, and a time to hate; a time of war, and a time of peace.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ECC.3.9",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ECC.3.9",
      "verse": 9,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "What profit hath he that worketh in that in which he laboreth?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ECC.3.10",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ECC.3.10",
      "verse": 10,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "I have seen the labor, which God hath given to the sons of men to be exercised in it.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ECC.3.11",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ECC.3.11",
      "verse": 11,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "He hath made every ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "thing",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " beautiful in its time: also he hath set the world in their heart, so that no man can find out the work that God maketh from the beginning to the end.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ECC.3.12",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ECC.3.12",
      "verse": 12,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "I know that ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "there is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " no good in them, but for ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "a man",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " to rejoice, and to do good in his life.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ECC.3.13",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ECC.3.13",
      "verse": 13,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And also that every man should eat and drink, and enjoy the good of all his labor, it ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " the gift of God.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ECC.3.14",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ECC.3.14",
      "verse": 14,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "I know that, whatever God doeth, it shall be for ever: nothing can be added to it, nor any thing taken from it: and God doeth ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "it",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": ", that ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "men",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " should fear before him.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ECC.3.15",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ECC.3.15",
      "verse": 15,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "That which hath been is now; and that which is to be hath already been; and God requireth that which is past.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ECC.3.16",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ECC.3.16",
      "verse": 16,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And moreover I saw under the sun the place of judgment, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "that",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " wickedness ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "was",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " there; and the place of righteousness, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "that",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " iniquity ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "was",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " there.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ECC.3.17",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ECC.3.17",
      "verse": 17,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "I said in my heart, God will judge the righteous and the wicked: for ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "there is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " a time there for every purpose and for every work.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ECC.3.18",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ECC.3.18",
      "verse": 18,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "I said in my heart concerning the state of the sons of men, that God might manifest them, and that they might see that they themselves are beasts.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ECC.3.19",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ECC.3.19",
      "verse": 19,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For that which befalleth the sons of men befalleth beasts; even one thing befalleth them: as the one dieth, so dieth the other; yes, they have all one breath; so that a man hath no pre-eminence above a beast: for all ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " vanity.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ECC.3.20",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ECC.3.20",
      "verse": 20,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "All go to one place; all are of the dust, and all turn to dust again.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ECC.3.21",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ECC.3.21",
      "verse": 21,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Who knoweth the spirit of man that goeth upward, and the spirit of the beast that goeth downward to the earth?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ECC.3.22",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ECC.3.22",
      "verse": 22,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Wherefore I perceive that ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "there is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " nothing better, than that a man should rejoice in his own works; for that ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " his portion: for who shall bring him to see what shall be after him?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    }
  ]
}
